ReShade shader API header fetched for the ReShade effect catalog

Source: crosire/reshade-shaders, Shaders/ReShade.fxh, pinned commit
fd0022170615ce0d8162d219bff07232fa6dd84f.
The upstream file identifies its license as SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0.
The header is fetched and integrity-checked during deployment; it is not
included in the release ZIP.

Third-party ReShade effects fetched on demand (not part of the Materials)

TeknoParrot Manager does not include these shaders in its release ZIP. When a user chooses a
profile, the program fetches the files below, unmodified, from the pinned upstream commit,
accepts them only when their SHA-256 and byte length match, and writes them to the user's own
ReShade folder together with a copy of the upstream license text where the upstream project
supplies one and a short TeknoParrot notice (Shaders\TPM\Notices\<effect>\). Each effect remains
under its own license; nothing in this file relicenses it, and the restrictions above apply only to
the Materials. The files are separate shader files loaded by ReShade; TeknoParrot Manager does not
edit them. An effect is offered by the program only while its recorded licence evidence (pinned bytes,
in-file notices or license copies, include closure) is complete and current.

