Licenses that carry conditions beyond keeping the notice:
- GPL-2.0-or-later: CRT-Royale (akgunter/crt-royale-reshade; several files are MIT per file) and CRT-Pi
  (Matsilagi/RSRetroArch; the in-file notice names davej, and the GPL text copy is the one distributed
  with crt-royale). GPL-3.0: the Lilium HDR shaders (oklab.fxh is MIT; darktable_ucs.fxh carries a
  copyright notice only and is covered by the project license). TeknoParrot Manager deploys these files
  unmodified, together with the license text and the pinned source location (Shaders/TPM/Notices/<EffectId>/NOTICE.txt),
  and modifies no covered file. This describes what the application does; it is not a legal opinion.
- CC BY-SA 4.0: FilmicAnamorphSharpen.fx (Jakub Maximilian Fober). Attribution stays in the unmodified
  file header; an adaptation must be shared under the same license. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
- BSD-2-Clause: AdaptiveSharpen.fx and Colourfulness.fx (bacondither); the license notice in each file is
  retained unchanged. MIT with a credit request: Deband.fx keeps its credit header unchanged.
- SMAA lookup textures (AreaTex.png, SearchTex.png) are covered by the SMAA project license (MIT, Jimenez et
  al.), whose LICENSE.txt (iryoku/smaa @ 71c806a838bdd7d517df19192a20f0c61b3ca29d) is copied beside them.
- Glamayre Fast Effects: MIT. Its depth-dependent features need compatible game depth data.
